hropic), facts (sonnet, anthropic); budget 12m. No cross-family spend consented.\nran: self: reported in 126s; facts: reported in 46s\nplan check: PASS \u2014 no deviation; the what is covered.\n\nFindings:\n1. verifiable \u00b7 README.md:20 \u00b7 \"Nuclear plants planned in PDP7A are replaced by coal\" is wrong against the code: plan_baseline.py:63 replaces Nuclear with Gas, and :210 says \"we replace nuclear with gas\". The README copied the stale docstring at plan_baseline.py:15 (\"Nuclear replaced by Coal\"). Fix: \"replaced by gas\" (and fix the docstring in a separate commit or ticket). The published paper says nothing either way.\n2. verifiable \u00b7 README.md:57 \u00b7 \"fitted on BP, IEA, and World Bank series\" is wrong: prices_data_international.py:12 names World Bank, BP and US EIA (not IEA), and only the World Bank file is active (:24-26), the BP and EIA blocks being commented out (:28-37). The student project agrees (World Bank used; BP and EIA compared). Suggest \"fitted on World Bank series; BP and EIA series are alternatives\".\n3. verifiable \u00b7 README.md:12 \u00b7 \"estimates the costs and CO2 emissions ... from 1975 to 2050\" overstates: costs, emissions and discounting run over START_YEAR..END_YEAR = 2016-2050 (init.py:64-66; Run.py:132). Only the capacity path goes back to 1975 (paper Fig. 3, plan_baseline.py:77). Suggest \"the costs and CO2 emissions ... from 2016 to 2050\", with capacities tracked from 1975.\n4. consider \u00b7 README.md:41 \u00b7 \"CCS deployed from about 2040\": gas CCS pilots come in 2024 and 2029 and the retrofit of coal and gas starts in 2035 (plan_with_ccs.py:62); captured CO2 is already 23 Mt in 2035. \"Scaled up from 2035\" fits better. The paper names this plan \"High CCS\" (the code's summary header too); \"With CCS\" matches the plan object and the paper's Fig. 3 caption, so either is defensible.\n5. consider \u00b7 README.md:56 \u00b7 the 100 trajectories are set in run_sensitivity_lcoe.py (multiple_LCOE(...,